#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Adds the Come Write With Me page to the Drafting Desk: a playlist-fed list of sessions, a pinned intro, and a newsletter card that says it is not open yet; and opens up the paper's drawing (no tape, padlock or cone).

Run it from the project folder, AFTER unzipping starscapes-come-write-19oct.zip into it:   python3 tools/add-come-write.py

What it does: it makes exact edits to ten files that already exist (the YouTube function and feed code, the Den's player, the Drafting Desk's routes and papers, the page titles, the paper's and the desk's drawings, the health check and its list of picture fingerprints) and adds four new files from the zip.
  api/youtube-series.js, lib/youtubeFeed.js, src/den/YouTubeSeriesPage.jsx, src/draftingdesk/DraftingDeskRoutes.jsx, src/draftingdesk/draftingData.js, src/data/pageMeta.js, public/scenes/drafting-desk/sheet-come-write-with-me.svg, public/scenes/drafting-desk/base.svg, tools/art-manifest.json, tools/health-check.mjs

How it keeps you safe:
  - It checks ALL 10 files first. If any is not exactly the way it expects, it changes NOTHING and says which.
  - Before changing a file it keeps a copy, ending .before-come-write.
  - It is safe to run twice: a file already done is left alone.
  - The new files (src/draftingdesk/comeWriteData.js, src/draftingdesk/comeWriteApi.js, src/draftingdesk/ComeWriteWithMePage.jsx, src/draftingdesk/comewrite.css) come in the zip itself.
"""
import json
import pathlib
import sys

